 "summary": "Mahagi territory part 1 (Mahagi, Logo, Nyarambe and Angumu health zones) is mostly Alur-majority and lies north/east of the Djugu Hema–Lendu conflict core. Mahagi town, the Uganda border/lake port and Logo/Nyarambe are assessed as state-held (PNC with FARDC). The southern Angumu area and the western Rimba/Aungba fringe border CODECO zones and suffer incursions; FARDC is assessed as the main force there. NOTE: no web research could be done for this unit (search budget exhausted, sites blocked); all zones are default-presence or low-confidence inferences and should be re-checked. Reviewer note (2026-10-01): independent review also could not run web searches or fetch news sites (search budget exhausted, egress blocked); zones were checked only for internal consistency and against the neighbouring Djugu and Mahagi-2 assessments. The cited sources (s1-s3) are generic portals, not specific reports.",
